---
title: Your account — FrontierJS Supply Co.
description: Sign in to see what you have ordered.
render: static
---
<!--
  The account page, and there is no `index.meta.js` beside it — deliberately.

  Every other route here has a `load()` that reads the catalogue at build time,
  and the build proves what it published. This one reads NOTHING at build time
  and could not: whose account it is is not known until a browser opens it, and
  `Order` is `@@gate("1.4.4.5")` now, so a `load()` that asked would be refused
  by the publish check rather than by anything at runtime — which is the check
  working, on the one page where it would have mattered most.

  So the file that ships is a heading and a mount point. Everything else is the
  island, which signs in on this origin and asks the API as that person.
-->
<script>
  import Account from '../../islands/Account.mesa'
</script>

<div class="container stack">
  <header class="stack">
    <h1>Your account</h1>
    <p class="text-muted">
      Orders you have placed with us, and what was in them.
    </p>
  </header>

  <Account client:load />
</div>
